# swing-edge.xrs - the motion sword (VR-37): does swinging the right controller
# swing the sword, and does ordinary hand movement leave it alone?
#
# Needs: a loaded level in GAMEPLAY (not a menu, not the title's attract scene -
# look at an xrsim-shot first), [Mode] GamepadOnly=0, and a build that has the
# `swing` word. Run:  .\tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path .\tools\xrsim\swing-edge.xrs
#
# How to read a failure: every `swing: BLOCKED` line names the gate that closed,
# and `swing status` (tools\game-cmd.ps1 "swing status") prints the gate, the
# counters and the PEAK speed. A FIRE with no HONOURED line means the pulse
# reached the pad and the game did not start an attack; the NOT HONOURED line
# says which of the two known reasons it looks like.
#
# The hand is only ever MOVED here, never placed: `hand r grip pose` teleports it,
# and a teleport is a tracking jump, which the detector discards on purpose.

# The sword has to be in the hand. With it sheathed the first pull draws it; with
# it drawn this is one ordinary attack. Either way the sword is out afterwards.
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 1200
@wait 1500
trigger r pull 300
@wait 2500
@mod swing on; swing mode edge; swing threshold 3.6; swing rearm 1.0; swing cooldown 300; swing rel on; swing sword on; swing output rt
@wait 1000
@mark

# 1. A reach is not a swing: 0.68 m in 900 ms peaks near 1.1 m/s.
hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 900
@wait 1600
@nolog swing: FIRE
@modassert features.swing.peakSpeed10s lt 3.6
@modassert features.swing.gateOpen eq true

# 2. A swing is: the same 0.68 m in 200 ms peaks near 5 m/s. One attack, and the
#    game has to be SEEN starting it - the pulse reaching the pad proves nothing.
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 200
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ slash
@log swing: HONOURED slash
@wait 1200
@nolog swing: FIRE
@modassert features.swing.notHonoured eq 0

# 3. Back the other way: the latch re-armed while the hand rested.
hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 200
@log swing: FIRE #\d+ slash
@log swing: HONOURED slash
@wait 1200

# 4. Turning the whole body is not a swing: head and hand move together.
@mark
head to 0.60 1.60 0 0 0 0 200; hand r to grip 0.25 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 200
@wait 1200
@nolog swing: FIRE
head to 0 1.60 0 0 0 0 1500; hand r to grip -0.35 1.00 -0.45 0 0 0 1500
@wait 2000

# 5. Three simulated swings through the real decision core and the real gates.
@mark
@mod swing sim 5 200 3
@log swing: sim window finished: 3 fire 8s
hand r to grip 0.25 1.30 -0.40 0 0 0 1200
